# Bench output — scripts write here, and a TRACKED output directory means every
# floor run dirties the repo. That is how F-14.14 happened: a `git add -A` over a
# floor-dirtied tree staged ten tracked artifacts as DELETIONS in an unintended
# commit. Ignoring it also turns the post-run dirt check in run-floor.sh into a
# real guard: with this line, any dirt after a floor means a bench left
# PRODUCTION SOURCE mutated. The untracking is the founder's own paste block —
# its own step, because the apply chain cannot delete.
scripts/out/
